  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Forced Displacement and Return of Afghans</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency assistance to unprecedented numbers of families returning to Afghanistan from neighbouring Pakistan and Iran through direct food, health, shelter and reintegration support. More than 1.5m people have crossed into Afghanistan since January with the daily number of returnees surging after 13 June, peaking on 1 July when over 43,000 people were registered in a single day from Iran alone, accompanied by thousands crossing daily from Pakistan. If current trends continue, Afghanistan could see over three million returnees by the end of 2025. This represents the largest and underreported acute migration emergency in the world. Compounded by the ongoing humanitarian crisis in Afghanistan where more than half of the population live in extreme poverty and women and girls are subjected to strict legal restrictions on movement, health and education.&#xa0;
Project will be implemented through collaboration with IFRC (Livelihood and Multipurpose Cash Assistance, MPCA) &amp; Norwegian Red Cross (Health)</narrative>
  </description>
